  "comment": "Fictional Codex process tables and homes shared by the parity check. tests/mesh-sessions-codex-parity.test.ts writes each scenario as a fake /proc (bind-mounted on /proc in a user and mount namespace) and a home, runs discover.codex_info on the labelled processes in one listing scope, then drop_duplicate_guessed_ids, and compares with golden.json; test_codex_parity.ml runs the Codex adapter on the same scenario through a fictional platform. Times are ages in seconds before the listing's 'now'. Every scenario also has pid 1 (systemd, cwd /), 50 (bash, cwd $W) and 60 (bash, cwd /). In strings, $W is the scenario's work folder, $A $B $C conversation ids and $A_UPPER the first in upper case; the argv word $TAIL is the options the mesh adds to a launch. A rollout is ~/.codex/sessions/<day>/rollout-<name>.jsonl, first line a session_meta with id, cwd and source, then 'lines' (an object is written as JSON, a string as it is, {\"hex\": ...} as raw bytes). fd_state: ok, unreadable (its fd entry is not a directory), vanished (no fd entry: it exited), denied (unreadable, and the process is this user's: a non-dumpable process).",
